  "label": "User projected onto the textual metaphor implying racial incompatibility",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'farm equipment and livestock don't mix', which functions as a deictic metaphor that directs the viewer to interpret the visual scene (the interracial couple) through the lens of racial incompatibility. The meme implicitly invites the user to see the couple as an unnatural or unsuitable pairing, aligning with the user's own social or cultural biases regarding interracial relationships. There are no explicit deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but the metaphorical framing projects the user's potential judgment or societal norms onto the couple.",
